# ---- Critical services: why they must never be stopped or disabled
crit.RpcSs = Remote Procedure Call (RPC): core of COM/RPC, Windows stops working
crit.RpcEptMapper = RPC Endpoint Mapper: essential for RPC
crit.DcomLaunch = DCOM Server Process Launcher: core of COM
crit.LSM = Local Session Manager: without it there are no user sessions
crit.BrokerInfrastructure = Background Tasks Infrastructure: required by the system and apps
crit.SamSs = Security Accounts Manager: needed to sign in
crit.ProfSvc = User Profile Service: without it nobody can sign in
crit.UserManager = User Manager: Start menu, sign-in and apps
crit.PlugPlay = Plug and Play: hardware detection and configuration
crit.Power = Power: system power management
crit.EventLog = Windows Event Log: many services depend on it
crit.Schedule = Task Scheduler: runs system maintenance tasks
crit.Winmgmt = Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI)
crit.gpsvc = Group Policy Client: policies and security settings
crit.CoreMessagingRegistrar = CoreMessaging: internal user-interface communication
crit.SystemEventsBroker = System Events Broker: triggers for tasks and apps
crit.TimeBrokerSvc = Time Broker: triggers for background tasks
crit.StateRepository = State Repository Service: Start menu and apps
crit.CryptSvc = Cryptographic Services: signatures, certificates and Windows Update
crit.KeyIso = CNG Key Isolation: credentials and encryption
crit.VaultSvc = Credential Manager: sign-in for apps and services
crit.Appinfo = Application Information: UAC elevation (Run as administrator)
crit.EventSystem = COM+ Event System: required by many services
crit.Dhcp = DHCP Client: network configuration (also used with a static IP)
crit.Dnscache = DNS Client: name resolution
crit.nsi = Network Store Interface Service: foundation of networking
crit.NlaSvc = Network Location Awareness: network detection
crit.netprofm = Network List Service: network profiles
crit.Wcmsvc = Windows Connection Manager: network connections
crit.BFE = Base Filtering Engine: firewall, IPsec and network security
crit.mpssvc = Windows Defender Firewall: protection, and required by many apps
crit.msiserver = Windows Installer: installing, repairing and removing programs
crit.TrustedInstaller = Windows Modules Installer: updates and components
crit.sppsvc = Software Protection: Windows licensing and activation

